      "evidence": "template/scripts/_platform_common.py lifecycle_mode: `if not isinstance(version, str) or not version: raise PlatformConfigError(...)`. The template .dev-platform.toml.jinja:2 writes platform_version, so new renders are fine. The diff has no upgrade or migration path or test for legacy configs, and design.md does not discuss it.",
      "id": "missing-platform-version-hard-fails-legacy-contracts",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "lifecycle_mode raises PlatformConfigError when platform_version is absent. It is now called unconditionally at the start of finish_task.main, project_publish.main, requirement_terminal.reconcile_parent, execute_requirement.advance and requirement_integration.publish_candidate. Older downstream renders or hand-edited contracts without that key would fail every one of these entrypoints. Previously they ran with config.get('platform_version') != 'source'."
